{"id": 473496, "platform": 19, "release_region": {"id": 2, "region": "north_america"}}, {"id": 545230, "date": 724032000, "platform": 58, "y": 1992, "release_region": {"id": 5, "region": "japan"}}, {"id": 797544, "date": 1757030400, "platform": 130, "y": 2025, "release_region": {"id": 8, "region": "worldwide"}}, {"id": 797545, "date": 1757030400, "platform": 6, "y": 2025, "release_region": {"id": 8, "region": "worldwide"}}], "screenshots": [{"id": 704636, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/scf3p8.jpg"}, {"id": 704637, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/scf3p9.jpg"}, {"id": 1665847, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sczpdj.jpg"}, {"id": 704645, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/scf3ph.jpg"}, {"id": 704646, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/scf3pi.jpg"}, {"id": 704647, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/scf3pj.jpg"}, {"id": 704638, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/scf3pa.jpg"}, {"id": 704640, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/scf3pc.jpg"}, {"id": 704643, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/scf3pf.jpg"}, {"id": 704641, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/scf3pd.jpg"}, {"id": 704644, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/scf3pg.jpg"}, {"id": 704639, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/scf3pb.jpg"}, {"id": 704642, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/scf3pe.jpg"}], "slug": "psycho-dream", "storyline": "In the early 1980s, rumors begin to circulate about a new entertainment medium called \u201cD Movie\u201d, which allows people to immerse themselves in a world of virtual reality. As D Movies gain traction, a trend emerges of disaffected young people taking permanent refuge in the virtual world while abandoning their physical bodies to atrophy. To retrieve these so-called \u201cSinkers\u201d, Japan's National Public Safety Commission establishes Public Security Division Four, nicknamed \u201cDiamond Dog\u201d, in 1984. The agents who enter the virtual world and perform these rescues are known as Debuggers.\n\nIn 1992, a seventeen-year-old girl named Y\u016bki Sayaka sinks into \u201cStory of the Ruined Capital\u201d, a D Movie directed by David Visconti. Three days pass before she is discovered, and combined with her weak constitution, she is expected to die within twenty-four hours. Two Debuggers, Shijima Ry\u014d and Tobari Maria, are dispatched to rescue her before that happens.", "summary": "Psycho Dream is a side-scrolling action platform game developed by Riot, a division of Telenet Japan, for the Super Famicom. Set in a virtual-reality medium called D-Movie, the story follows two agents, Ry\u014d Shijima and Maria Tobari, who enter a dream world to rescue a girl trapped there.\n\nPlayers can choose between Ry\u014d, who fights with a sword, and Maria, who uses ranged and transformation-based attacks. The game is structured around short action stages with enemies, hazards, and boss encounters, combining science fiction and horror imagery. It was released in Japan in 1992, while a planned North American release under the title Dream Probe was not completed.", "themes": [{"id": 1, "name": "Action"}, {"id": 18, "name": "Science fiction"}], "url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/psycho-dream", "videos": [{"id": 62757, "name": "Gameplay Video", "video_id": "UlKH1_estpw", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UlKH1_estpw", "title": "SNES Longplay [197] Psycho Dream", "thumb": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/UlKH1_estpw/hqdefault.jpg"}]}